0001 — classlink.rs: `zend_traits_init_trait_structures` (resolution and
validation of `insteadof` / `as` rules) and "cannot use X - it is not a
trait" as an Error exception.

php-src resolves the trait named by every precedence and alias rule at link
time, in two passes (all `insteadof` rules first, then all `as` rules), with
`zend_hash_find_ptr_lc(EG(class_table))` (no autoloading), and raises
E_COMPILE_ERROR at the class declaration line for:
  "Could not find trait %s",
  "Class %s is not a trait, Only traits may be used in 'as' and 'insteadof' statements",
  "Required Trait %s wasn't added to %s",
  "A precedence rule was defined for %s::%s but this method does not exist",
  "Failed to evaluate a trait precedence (%s). Method of trait %s was defined to be excluded multiple times",
  "Inconsistent insteadof definition. The method %s is to be used from %s, but %s is also on the exclude list",
  "An alias was defined for %s::%s but this method does not exist",
  "An alias was defined for method %s(), which exists in both %s and %s. Use %s::%s or %s::%s to resolve the ambiguity",
  "An alias (%s) was defined for method %s(), but this method does not exist",
  "The modifiers of the trait method %s() are changed, but this method does not exist. Error".
An unqualified `as` rule applies to the one trait that has the method (the
old code applied it to every trait with that name). Duplicated trait uses
are skipped (`zend_do_link_class`). `zend_do_link_class` throws
`Error("%s cannot use %s - it is not a trait")` rather than a fatal error.
The resolved rules (`TraitRules`: excluded (trait index, method) pairs and
the trait index of each alias rule) are passed to build_class.

Fixes Zend/tests/traits: bug54441, bug60165a, bug60165b, bug60165c,
bug60165d, bug61052, bug62069, bug62069_2, bug63219, bug64235, bug64235b,
error_003, error_004, error_005, error_006, error_010, language015,
language016, language017, precedence_unknown_class (20 tests).
(The only other hunk is rustfmt of the zend_implement_serializable condition.)

